1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,102
What?
Make sure they will be there later, okay?

2
00:00:02,102 --> 00:00:05,405
Siloy's wife said
she'd meet you at the morgue.

3
00:00:05,405 --> 00:00:08,842
- Morgue?
- She said Siloy's dead.

4
00:00:11,934 --> 00:00:14,370
Siloy!

5
00:00:14,370 --> 00:00:16,213
- Son of a...
- Are you going to tell us the truth?

6
00:00:16,213 --> 00:00:20,377
Or should I bring your young daughter here?

7
00:00:20,377 --> 00:00:24,095
Leave my daughter out of it!

8
00:00:25,649 --> 00:00:30,154
Even the best film has an ending.

9
00:00:30,154 --> 00:00:33,790
Not all can be done with magic.

10
00:00:33,790 --> 00:00:36,218
<i>Your dad collapsed in his house!</i>

11
00:00:36,218 --> 00:00:39,330
I'm sorry, my dear.

12
00:00:39,330 --> 00:00:42,262
- I thought you quit already?
- What matters is you're safe.

13
00:00:42,262 --> 00:00:43,801
Get well, okay?

14
00:00:43,801 --> 00:00:46,203
- Do you want to see her?
- I'm busy here.

15
00:00:46,203 --> 00:00:48,739
- I've got work to do.
- Hey.

16
00:00:48,739 --> 00:00:49,807
Go.

17
00:00:49,807 --> 00:00:51,608
Are you just going to let him go, Miss?

18
00:00:51,608 --> 00:00:56,012
I also want to make sure
if he still knows his way back home.

19
00:00:58,373 --> 00:00:59,744
Liam.

20
00:01:22,806 --> 00:01:24,641
Vergil.

21
00:01:27,848 --> 00:01:30,283
What is Vergil doing here?

22
00:01:37,204 --> 00:01:40,740
You and your sons are testing my patience.

23
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:46,331
Danilo, it was Liam who approached me.

24
00:01:46,331 --> 00:01:52,036
He said he needed money
for his mom's operation.

25
00:01:55,073 --> 00:01:58,425
And because he is Via's boyfriend,

26
00:01:58,425 --> 00:02:01,045
I let him join my business.

27
00:02:01,813 --> 00:02:06,217
And now you're going to tag Vergil along?

28
00:02:08,586 --> 00:02:11,388
- You are like leeches.
- Uncle!

29
00:02:13,992 --> 00:02:15,126
Uncle...

30
00:02:15,126 --> 00:02:18,329
Kneel down when you're talking to him.

31
00:02:20,981 --> 00:02:22,968
Uncle...

32
00:02:22,968 --> 00:02:25,937
Dad didn't know I followed him.

33
00:02:25,937 --> 00:02:28,005
Punish me instead.

34
00:02:28,807 --> 00:02:31,475
Vergil, stay out of this.

35
00:02:34,832 --> 00:02:37,568
What do you know about this business?

36
00:02:40,618 --> 00:02:44,556
Uncle, this isn't new to me.

37
00:02:44,556 --> 00:02:47,125
I'm now a part of it.

38
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:49,961
But please, not my dad.

39
00:02:49,961 --> 00:02:52,297
Let him work at Casa Fuerte.

40
00:02:52,297 --> 00:02:55,466
I can be your right-hand man.

41
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:05,943
Big bro, what do I do with these two?

42
00:03:20,022 --> 00:03:23,461
He said he wanted to be my right-hand man.

43
00:03:23,461 --> 00:03:25,663
Give it a try.

44
00:03:25,663 --> 00:03:27,608
Uncle!

45
00:03:32,704 --> 00:03:34,672
Thank you, Uncle Ramon.

46
00:03:34,672 --> 00:03:36,807
I won't disappoint you.

47
00:03:44,215 --> 00:03:46,351
You heard Uncle Ramon, right?

48
00:03:46,351 --> 00:03:48,186
I'm now his right-hand man.

49
00:03:48,186 --> 00:03:49,721
Help me get up.

50
00:03:49,721 --> 00:03:52,090
Give me your right hand.

51
00:03:52,090 --> 00:03:54,423
He said right hand, right?

52
00:03:54,423 --> 00:03:56,027
Hey!

53
00:03:56,027 --> 00:03:57,995
Don't hurt him!

54
00:04:00,512 --> 00:04:02,403
That's enough!

55
00:04:15,713 --> 00:04:22,617
If only Joyce had listened to me,
you now would've been her boyfriend.

56
00:04:23,483 --> 00:04:24,883
- Auntie...
- Mommy.

57
00:04:25,757 --> 00:04:27,158
I'm not in a rush.

58
00:04:27,158 --> 00:04:31,734
I'm being a workaholic like her.

59
00:04:31,734 --> 00:04:33,898
Gosh.

60
00:04:33,898 --> 00:04:38,470
With the money you make
and your family's business,

61
00:04:38,470 --> 00:04:43,361
you can ask Joyce to quit acting. Right?

62
00:04:45,306 --> 00:04:48,413
Mommy, please, just eat.

63
00:04:48,413 --> 00:04:50,582
I'm on a diet.

64
00:04:50,582 --> 00:04:52,417
This is what I only eat.

65
00:04:58,356 --> 00:04:59,657
Hey.

66
00:04:59,657 --> 00:05:03,428
I'm waiting for an important email. Hey!

67
00:05:03,428 --> 00:05:04,963
Joyce.

68
00:05:04,963 --> 00:05:08,466
Finally, we already have a lead
to help with the investigation.

69
00:05:08,466 --> 00:05:12,170
The CCTV captured a man
when the crime happened, Auntie.

70
00:05:12,170 --> 00:05:15,140
That's not a good topic in the morning.

71
00:05:15,140 --> 00:05:16,341
It's not office hours yet.

72
00:05:16,341 --> 00:05:17,842
Look at the time.
There are still two minutes left.

73
00:05:17,842 --> 00:05:19,144
Eat.

74
00:05:19,144 --> 00:05:20,995
Eat first.

75
00:05:27,218 --> 00:05:31,489
Look at that. Look at your cell phones.

76
00:05:31,489 --> 00:05:35,326
Matchy-matchy. A match made in heaven.

77
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:38,530
Unlike Edmond and I.

78
00:05:38,530 --> 00:05:41,765
It's like dealing with a demon.

79
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:44,535
Mommy.

80
00:05:51,707 --> 00:05:53,878
Hello?

81
00:05:53,878 --> 00:05:56,767
Jana, good morning.

82
00:05:56,767 --> 00:05:57,801
So?

83
00:05:57,801 --> 00:06:03,571
There's no news
about Joyce's junkie father, right?

84
00:06:05,588 --> 00:06:07,158
That's good to hear.

85
00:06:07,158 --> 00:06:08,649
I'm glad.

86
00:06:14,186 --> 00:06:16,776
Thank you for the breakfast.

87
00:06:16,777 --> 00:06:19,416
Two minutes are over.

88
00:06:21,151 --> 00:06:25,454
You can't leave until you finish your food.

89
00:06:28,403 --> 00:06:29,856
Eat.

90
00:06:38,590 --> 00:06:41,261
Your suit will get stains.

91
00:06:43,094 --> 00:06:45,263
- Go on. You can leave now.
- Please.

92
00:06:45,263 --> 00:06:46,776
Go.

93
00:06:46,777 --> 00:06:49,412
- I only have a little leftover.
- Water.

94
00:06:52,570 --> 00:06:54,272
- Okay?
- Okay.

95
00:06:54,272 --> 00:06:55,640
Thank you, Auntie.

96
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:57,208
Thank you for the breakfast.

97
00:06:57,208 --> 00:06:59,043
Bye.

98
00:06:59,043 --> 00:07:01,546
Just be patient with my daughter.

99
00:07:01,546 --> 00:07:03,047
She'll say yes eventually.

100
00:07:03,047 --> 00:07:04,683
Mom...

101
00:07:05,583 --> 00:07:07,363
I hope so.

102
00:07:13,227 --> 00:07:15,126
How are you doing, Dad?

103
00:07:15,126 --> 00:07:17,843
I'm great.

104
00:07:17,843 --> 00:07:24,301
Our new counselor is good.
He's the one who encouraged me to...

105
00:07:25,169 --> 00:07:27,471
How should I say this?

106
00:07:28,673 --> 00:07:30,074
Dear...

107
00:07:32,243 --> 00:07:43,421
I want to tell you why I always return to...

108
00:07:43,421 --> 00:07:46,257
- to my old ways...
- Go ahead, Dad.

109
00:07:46,257 --> 00:07:48,392
I'll listen.

110
00:07:57,433 --> 00:07:59,501
Well, this is what happened.

111
00:08:01,105 --> 00:08:03,708
I met some people before.

112
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:07,220
Who is this?

113
00:08:13,685 --> 00:08:15,124
Hello?

114
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:19,355
Hello, sorry I can't take calls right now.

115
00:08:19,355 --> 00:08:22,030
<i>Attorney Hans, I sent you the video.</i>

116
00:08:22,030 --> 00:08:23,227
<i>I had it enhanced too.</i>

117
00:08:23,227 --> 00:08:24,495
Attorney Hans?

118
00:08:24,495 --> 00:08:26,030
<i>You can already see
the suspect's face on that copy.</i>

119
00:08:26,030 --> 00:08:28,066
This is Joyce.

120
00:08:28,066 --> 00:08:31,244
<i>Joyce? Why do you have Hans' phone?</i>

121
00:08:37,041 --> 00:08:38,343
Hello?

122
00:08:38,343 --> 00:08:40,044
Jayps?

123
00:08:40,044 --> 00:08:43,481
We switched our phones.

124
00:08:43,481 --> 00:08:47,650
I'm sorry. I'll bring his phone
to your office.

125
00:08:47,650 --> 00:08:51,354
<i>I'll tell him to find you when he gets here.</i>

126
00:08:52,190 --> 00:08:54,625
Okay, thank you.

127
00:09:03,131 --> 00:09:05,511
- Vergil.
- You, monster!

128
00:09:14,571 --> 00:09:16,439
Who is that?

129
00:09:20,747 --> 00:09:23,850
Someone sent a video.

130
00:09:23,850 --> 00:09:28,992
He's the suspect in the case
that Hans is investigating.

131
00:09:38,565 --> 00:09:40,002
Wait.

132
00:09:44,776 --> 00:09:46,944
I know that man.

133
00:09:46,944 --> 00:09:49,056
He finally admitted it.

134
00:09:52,350 --> 00:09:54,251
Do you know him, Dad?

135
00:09:55,653 --> 00:09:59,122
Dad, wait. How do you know this man?

136
00:09:59,791 --> 00:10:02,560
Dad, what is it that you're going to tell me?

137
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:04,634
Tell you?

138
00:10:04,634 --> 00:10:06,535
I'll tell you next time.

139
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:11,268
Dear, listen carefully.

140
00:10:12,637 --> 00:10:18,176
Don't get involved in Hans' investigation.

141
00:10:18,176 --> 00:10:19,744
They're dangerous.

142
00:10:19,744 --> 00:10:21,145
Okay?

143
00:10:21,145 --> 00:10:23,414
You better do this.

144
00:10:23,414 --> 00:10:25,416
- Dad...
- Warn Hans.

145
00:10:25,416 --> 00:10:29,053
Tell him to stop the investigation.

146
00:10:29,053 --> 00:10:30,655
- Okay?
- I don't get you, Dad.

147
00:10:30,655 --> 00:10:31,989
You'll get hurt.

148
00:10:31,989 --> 00:10:34,325
What's going on with you, Dad?

149
00:10:34,325 --> 00:10:36,060
Listen to me, Joyce.

150
00:10:36,060 --> 00:10:37,595
I don't understand.

151
00:10:37,595 --> 00:10:39,263
- It's an order. No, no.
- Sir, that's enough.

152
00:10:39,263 --> 00:10:40,598
Hold on.

153
00:10:40,598 --> 00:10:41,699
Wait!

154
00:10:41,699 --> 00:10:43,100
I'm protecting my daughter.

155
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:44,235
Dad, hold on.

156
00:10:44,235 --> 00:10:46,037
Wait a minute.

157
00:10:46,037 --> 00:10:48,439
Ma'am, we'll let him rest for now.

158
00:10:48,439 --> 00:10:49,841
Rest? What rest?

159
00:10:49,841 --> 00:10:51,175
I don't need rest.

160
00:10:51,175 --> 00:10:52,877
I'm her father.

161
00:10:52,877 --> 00:10:54,212
- Come on, let's go.
- I will protect her.

162
00:10:54,212 --> 00:10:55,613
Listen to me, Joyce.

163
00:10:55,613 --> 00:10:57,748
Do as I say.

164
00:10:57,748 --> 00:10:59,617
Stay away from those demons.

165
00:10:59,617 --> 00:11:00,852
Joyce!

166
00:11:00,852 --> 00:11:02,019
My child!

167
00:11:02,019 --> 00:11:04,721
They are demons!

168
00:11:10,126 --> 00:11:12,827
Calm down, you two.

169
00:11:14,532 --> 00:11:18,168
Vergil, why are you hurting your brother?

170
00:11:19,370 --> 00:11:21,672
Why do you have an arm sling?

171
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:25,008
What's happening?

172
00:11:28,646 --> 00:11:32,049
Mom, can you leave us alone for now?

173
00:11:32,049 --> 00:11:34,017
We need to talk.

174
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:37,221
No.

175
00:11:37,221 --> 00:11:39,123
I won't go anywhere.

176
00:11:39,123 --> 00:11:40,424
I'm your mom.

177
00:11:40,424 --> 00:11:44,237
I have the right to know
what's going on with the two of you.

178
00:11:46,130 --> 00:11:51,201
Vergil, I know you don't like me.

179
00:11:51,903 --> 00:11:55,940
But I never stopped being concerned
about you.

180
00:11:55,940 --> 00:11:58,909
You can ask Liam if you want.

181
00:11:59,651 --> 00:12:03,654
Now I want to know what trouble you have.

182
00:12:04,949 --> 00:12:08,085
What do you mean by
what you said earlier, Vergil?

183
00:12:08,085 --> 00:12:10,626
What did Liam do to Danilo?

184
00:12:10,626 --> 00:12:12,894
Come on. What's going on?

185
00:12:16,093 --> 00:12:18,369
I'm sorry, Aunt Tess.

186
00:12:19,297 --> 00:12:22,399
I lost my patience when I found out that...

187
00:12:25,303 --> 00:12:30,073
I found out that Liam left a huge debt
in Casa Fuerte.

188
00:12:30,841 --> 00:12:33,444
Dad told me.

189
00:12:33,444 --> 00:12:35,779
And now he's paying for it.

190
00:12:40,017 --> 00:12:41,852
Is that so?

191
00:12:44,121 --> 00:12:47,191
So, it's your fault, son.

192
00:12:47,191 --> 00:12:50,093
And I'm blaming your brother.

193
00:12:51,128 --> 00:12:53,965
Son, fix that problem.

194
00:12:53,965 --> 00:12:56,500
You should pay your father.

195
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:59,035
That's embarrassing.

196
00:13:02,287 --> 00:13:05,343
Oh, dear. Talk to each other decently.

197
00:13:05,343 --> 00:13:06,877
I'm going to leave you here.

198
00:13:06,877 --> 00:13:09,246
No fighting.

199
00:13:09,246 --> 00:13:11,114
Yes, Mom.

200
00:13:19,334 --> 00:13:21,037
Thank you.

201
00:13:22,193 --> 00:13:25,362
Thank you for keeping the truth from my mom.

202
00:13:26,497 --> 00:13:30,700
Can we talk somewhere else?

203
00:13:44,624 --> 00:13:46,450
Thank you.

204
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:48,185
We switched our phones.

205
00:13:48,185 --> 00:13:49,353
Hello.

206
00:13:49,353 --> 00:13:52,556
What's with the video that was sent to you?

207
00:13:52,556 --> 00:13:55,092
Video? What video?

208
00:13:55,092 --> 00:13:58,462
The video you're waiting for from Jayps.

209
00:13:58,462 --> 00:14:02,133
My dad saw the man in the video.
And he knows him.

210
00:14:02,133 --> 00:14:03,934
He knows him?

211
00:14:06,203 --> 00:14:08,706
That's good, Joyce.

212
00:14:08,706 --> 00:14:11,475
Where's Uncle Edmond? Can I talk to him?

213
00:14:11,475 --> 00:14:13,778
Because it will make my investigation easier.

214
00:14:13,778 --> 00:14:17,414
- Come on, let's see him.
- You can't talk to him, Hans.

215
00:14:18,382 --> 00:14:20,251
You know his condition.

216
00:14:20,251 --> 00:14:22,085
You can't do that.

217
00:14:24,455 --> 00:14:26,135
I'll find the right time.

218
00:14:26,135 --> 00:14:28,370
I'll try to ask him.

219
00:14:33,764 --> 00:14:35,765
I'm sorry, Joyce.

220
00:14:36,801 --> 00:14:43,073
Maybe he's the key
to giving my client justice.

221
00:14:44,075 --> 00:14:46,977
If there's someone who has to pay
for what happened.

222
00:14:48,493 --> 00:14:51,462
You don't know how big this case is.

223
00:14:59,023 --> 00:15:01,358
Stay away from those demons!

224
00:15:01,358 --> 00:15:03,761
They're evil, Joyce!

225
00:15:03,761 --> 00:15:04,762
My child!

226
00:15:04,762 --> 00:15:07,731
They are demons!

227
00:15:09,467 --> 00:15:11,836
See what you did?

228
00:15:11,836 --> 00:15:15,503
Dad is paying for your mistakes.

229
00:15:15,503 --> 00:15:17,675
Dad is now managing
Uncle Ramon's transactions.

230
00:15:17,675 --> 00:15:19,809
The job you left.

231
00:15:21,445 --> 00:15:23,314
Transactions?

232
00:15:23,314 --> 00:15:26,684
Uncle Ramon's illegal money.

233
00:15:26,684 --> 00:15:29,153
Drugs, gambling dens, illegal weapons.

234
00:15:29,153 --> 00:15:32,756
He puts all the money in Casa Fuerte
to launder it.

235
00:15:35,359 --> 00:15:37,327
Money laundering?

236
00:15:39,029 --> 00:15:43,868
You know what, Liam?
You're the dumbest in the family.

237
00:15:43,868 --> 00:15:46,737
You have nothing to brag about.

238
00:15:46,737 --> 00:15:51,574
I'll do everything to get you and dad
out of this trouble.

239
00:15:51,574 --> 00:15:54,476
- I'll talk to Uncle Ramon.
- It's too late.

240
00:15:55,605 --> 00:15:59,083
Dad and I already know a lot.

241
00:15:59,083 --> 00:16:00,651
But you...

242
00:16:00,651 --> 00:16:03,487
Uncle Ramon let you go because of Via.

243
00:16:03,487 --> 00:16:05,822
So fix your life.

244
00:16:06,824 --> 00:16:09,658
And stay with Via.

245
00:16:09,658 --> 00:16:12,505
Because the moment you break up with her,

246
00:16:12,505 --> 00:16:14,665
you'll be dead.

247
00:16:14,665 --> 00:16:17,334
And so will everyone who matters to you.

248
00:16:17,334 --> 00:16:19,670
Do you understand?

249
00:16:19,670 --> 00:16:25,141
End whatever's going on
between you and Joyce.

250
00:16:26,010 --> 00:16:27,550
Bro...

251
00:16:30,647 --> 00:16:34,217
I grew up getting mad
whenever you'd call me brother.

252
00:16:35,352 --> 00:16:39,155
But this will be the only time
I'll be your big brother.

253
00:16:40,191 --> 00:16:42,459
Get your act together.

254
00:16:42,459 --> 00:16:44,561
Fix your relationship with Via.

255
00:16:45,763 --> 00:16:48,098
She's the only protection you have.

256
00:17:10,054 --> 00:17:12,122
My friend...

257
00:17:12,122 --> 00:17:16,026
do I really have to learn this?

258
00:17:16,794 --> 00:17:18,929
Yes.

259
00:17:18,929 --> 00:17:22,532
So that if your sons fail...

260
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:25,969
you'll be the one to shoot them.

261
00:17:26,971 --> 00:17:29,752
And if you fail...

262
00:17:29,752 --> 00:17:32,409
you'll have to shoot yourself.

263
00:17:32,409 --> 00:17:34,544
Come on, my friend.

264
00:17:37,014 --> 00:17:39,049
I'm not kidding.

265
00:17:40,651 --> 00:17:43,254
You would rather take a bullet

266
00:17:43,254 --> 00:17:48,992
than suffer my punishment
if you put me in trouble, Danilo.

267
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:54,402
How's Liam?

268
00:17:55,432 --> 00:17:58,635
I let him do the things he wants.

269
00:18:00,037 --> 00:18:02,238
Make a movie?

270
00:18:03,274 --> 00:18:06,776
He even dragged my daughter into it.

271
00:18:07,544 --> 00:18:11,482
It's fine, if only he's not cheating on Via.

272
00:18:11,482 --> 00:18:13,817
What do you mean?

273
00:18:13,817 --> 00:18:16,620
Liam loves Via so much.

274
00:18:16,620 --> 00:18:18,788
Fix my target.

275
00:18:23,173 --> 00:18:25,074
Fix it.

276
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:46,810
Intoy...

277
00:18:47,952 --> 00:18:53,723
What do you do
when problems keep coming your way?

278
00:18:55,492 --> 00:18:57,294
Nothing.

279
00:18:57,294 --> 00:19:00,497
I let the problem worry about me.

280
00:19:02,633 --> 00:19:04,934
Can't you loosen up a bit?

281
00:19:05,769 --> 00:19:07,804
Looks like it's serious.

282
00:19:10,941 --> 00:19:12,362
Dude...

283
00:19:13,310 --> 00:19:18,581
People deal with problems differently.

284
00:19:19,550 --> 00:19:24,120
But most of the time,
they choose the easiest way.

285
00:19:24,722 --> 00:19:26,323
Running away.

286
00:19:26,323 --> 00:19:32,629
But some choose the wrong path.

287
00:19:32,629 --> 00:19:39,869
Or some focus on other things.

288
00:19:40,971 --> 00:19:44,674
Sometimes people lack courage...

289
00:19:45,309 --> 00:19:48,278
Courage to deal with their problems.

290
00:19:52,649 --> 00:19:56,886
Oftentimes, the solution is within our reach.

291
00:19:58,555 --> 00:20:01,324
But we are taken over by fear.

292
00:20:12,770 --> 00:20:15,572
I understand everything you told me, Intoy.

293
00:20:18,509 --> 00:20:24,514
I just don't want my problems
to cause harm to others...

294
00:20:26,683 --> 00:20:29,219
Especially my loved ones.

295
00:20:51,107 --> 00:20:53,009
Why did you do that?

296
00:20:53,819 --> 00:20:55,954
Are you going to kill me?

297
00:20:57,381 --> 00:20:59,950
If you were my target,

298
00:20:59,950 --> 00:21:02,585
you wouldn't be able to talk anymore.

299
00:21:04,455 --> 00:21:07,958
Do you know what I told Liam?

300
00:21:07,958 --> 00:21:12,296
If he goes against me,
he's not the one who will get hurt.

301
00:21:12,296 --> 00:21:15,765
It's the people who matter to him.

302
00:21:27,858 --> 00:21:29,491
Why?

303
00:21:30,698 --> 00:21:32,553
Is it because of this?

304
00:21:33,484 --> 00:21:37,086
Do you think Liam and Joyce have an affair?

305
00:21:37,921 --> 00:21:40,290
It's just a film.

306
00:21:40,290 --> 00:21:42,458
They don't have a relationship.

307
00:21:45,061 --> 00:21:52,201
My daughter and I are not
the kind of people you can fool.

308
00:21:53,537 --> 00:21:55,639
And once I confirm

309
00:21:55,639 --> 00:22:02,178
that Liam is just using me
and my daughter... I'm sorry.

310
00:22:04,181 --> 00:22:07,283
Your clan will end with him.

311
00:22:14,358 --> 00:22:16,539
- Director Phil, everything is set.
- Okay.

312
00:22:16,539 --> 00:22:21,632
Josh, Joyce, can we do it in one take?

313
00:22:21,632 --> 00:22:23,200
Sure.

314
00:22:23,200 --> 00:22:25,601
We always do it in one take.

315
00:22:30,474 --> 00:22:32,242
Warn Hans.

316
00:22:32,242 --> 00:22:35,812
Tell him to stop investigating.

317
00:22:35,812 --> 00:22:37,381
- Okay?
- Dad, I can't understand.

318
00:22:37,381 --> 00:22:38,982
You'll only get in trouble.

319
00:22:38,982 --> 00:22:40,317
Where's Uncle Edmond?

320
00:22:40,317 --> 00:22:41,685
Can I talk to him?

321
00:22:41,685 --> 00:22:45,389
It will make my investigation easier.

322
00:22:45,389 --> 00:22:46,937
Joyce?

323
00:22:47,692 --> 00:22:49,159
Joyce?

324
00:22:49,159 --> 00:22:50,523
Hey.

325
00:22:51,828 --> 00:22:53,363
I don't think we can do it in one take.

326
00:22:53,363 --> 00:22:56,233
Sorry, Director Phil. Yes.

327
00:22:56,233 --> 00:22:59,035
Sorry, where were we?

328
00:23:01,038 --> 00:23:03,740
We're just here.

329
00:23:03,740 --> 00:23:07,410
But I don't know where you are.

330
00:23:08,579 --> 00:23:10,680
You're zoning out.

331
00:23:12,388 --> 00:23:14,856
Is something bothering you, Joyce?

332
00:23:16,086 --> 00:23:18,187
Nothing, Josh. I'm okay.

333
00:23:21,690 --> 00:23:27,205
Sir Liam, the stunt man we had last time
didn't return.

334
00:23:27,205 --> 00:23:29,499
What do we do with continuity?

335
00:23:35,539 --> 00:23:39,609
Sir Liam.

336
00:23:42,279 --> 00:23:44,347
C-Come again?

337
00:23:47,070 --> 00:23:50,887
Deedee, it's okay. I had him picked up.

338
00:23:50,887 --> 00:23:54,324
Sir Liam, everything's okay.

339
00:23:54,324 --> 00:23:55,770
Okay.

340
00:23:58,061 --> 00:24:01,022
Are you okay, Sir Liam?

341
00:24:01,022 --> 00:24:03,291
I'm okay. Don't worry about me.

342
00:24:05,435 --> 00:24:08,005
Okay. I'll be right there
if you need anything.

343
00:24:08,005 --> 00:24:09,634
Okay.

344
00:24:12,073 --> 00:24:13,811
Coffee!

345
00:24:13,811 --> 00:24:16,872
To wake you up, Boss Bro.

346
00:24:17,917 --> 00:24:20,119
You seem lost.

347
00:24:20,917 --> 00:24:22,619
Miss Joyce...

348
00:24:22,619 --> 00:24:24,087
There.

349
00:24:24,087 --> 00:24:25,922
So you can come back to earth.

350
00:24:25,922 --> 00:24:29,792
Your mind is somewhere else.

351
00:24:35,599 --> 00:24:37,066
Joyce...

352
00:24:37,886 --> 00:24:41,505
Are you sure you can start now?

353
00:24:41,505 --> 00:24:43,773
How about you? Are you ready?

354
00:24:44,975 --> 00:24:45,976
Sorry.

355
00:24:45,976 --> 00:24:47,778
I'm so sorry, I'm late.

356
00:24:47,778 --> 00:24:50,089
Did you already start?

357
00:24:52,013 --> 00:24:55,251
Someone got here at the same time I did.

358
00:24:58,188 --> 00:24:59,222
Hello.

359
00:24:59,222 --> 00:25:01,316
Hello, everyone.

360
00:25:01,316 --> 00:25:04,909
I'm glad to be part of your movie.

361
00:25:05,996 --> 00:25:07,664
Joyce, really?

362
00:25:07,664 --> 00:25:10,199
We're going to work with Maxine?

363
00:25:13,036 --> 00:25:19,476
Miss Lemon asked us
to include her in our project.

364
00:25:19,476 --> 00:25:23,714
Isn't she the one your fans suspect
to be your online basher?

365
00:25:23,714 --> 00:25:27,183
Isn't she the Girl with the Periwinkle Hair?

366
00:25:28,151 --> 00:25:31,521
We don't have any concrete evidence for that.

367
00:25:32,222 --> 00:25:35,559
I don't want any problems on my set.

368
00:25:35,559 --> 00:25:37,828
We're going to shoot the final sequence.

369
00:25:37,828 --> 00:25:40,796
It should be perfect.

370
00:25:46,937 --> 00:25:49,072
Joyce.

371
00:25:49,072 --> 00:25:50,873
Maxine.

372
00:26:07,591 --> 00:26:11,228
- Cindy.
- I'm so tired.

373
00:26:11,228 --> 00:26:14,131
Cindy.

374
00:26:14,131 --> 00:26:16,399
I'm so tired.

375
00:26:18,978 --> 00:26:22,505
I thought we would both find
a way to save our relationship.

376
00:26:22,505 --> 00:26:24,869
- But why is this happening?
- No.

377
00:26:25,884 --> 00:26:27,384
Cindy.

378
00:26:41,158 --> 00:26:44,130
Sorry if you got tired.

379
00:26:46,461 --> 00:26:49,364
Sorry if you feel alone.

380
00:27:02,612 --> 00:27:04,614
This is what I only got.

381
00:27:08,299 --> 00:27:14,838
I'm sorry if you got dragged
into my miserable life.

382
00:27:17,894 --> 00:27:23,032
I will understand if you want to leave me.

383
00:27:29,743 --> 00:27:31,877
Am I alone?

384
00:27:35,145 --> 00:27:38,114
Am I the only one willing to fight?

385
00:27:41,327 --> 00:27:43,395
I love you...

386
00:27:44,921 --> 00:27:46,822
So much.

387
00:27:47,524 --> 00:27:50,206
That's why I want you to be happy.

388
00:27:51,595 --> 00:27:57,567
Do you think I'm happy
with what's happening to us?

389
00:27:57,567 --> 00:27:59,735
I don't want to be selfish.

390
00:28:01,404 --> 00:28:03,506
I don't want to have you...

391
00:28:04,499 --> 00:28:07,001
and trap you in this relationship.

392
00:28:08,712 --> 00:28:11,703
I know...

393
00:28:14,206 --> 00:28:18,169
that I hurt you over and over again.

394
00:28:26,263 --> 00:28:28,164
I'm sorry.

395
00:28:57,527 --> 00:29:02,933
Love, the clothes that
Director Phil requested have arrived.

396
00:29:02,933 --> 00:29:08,404
And I ordered takeout
from our favorite restaurant.

397
00:29:12,527 --> 00:29:14,277
Sorry.

398
00:29:14,277 --> 00:29:19,950
While I'm still perfecting
Aunt Tess' recipes,

399
00:29:19,950 --> 00:29:23,419
have some of the takeout food first.

400
00:29:27,036 --> 00:29:29,872
Yummy. Do you want some rice?

401
00:29:34,264 --> 00:29:36,065
I'll get you some.

402
00:29:40,303 --> 00:29:41,602
Let's eat, love.

403
00:29:41,602 --> 00:29:45,834
Sorry, I should send this to
our film director before the break ends.

404
00:29:45,834 --> 00:29:47,877
What?

405
00:29:47,877 --> 00:29:53,116
We have breaks so we can eat.

406
00:29:53,116 --> 00:29:55,485
Come on.

407
00:29:55,485 --> 00:29:57,623
Have a break.

408
00:29:57,623 --> 00:29:59,355
Here.

409
00:30:03,893 --> 00:30:06,896
You know I don't eat that.

410
00:30:06,896 --> 00:30:08,584
Sorry, love.

411
00:30:15,905 --> 00:30:17,607
- Via.
- Go on. Try it.

412
00:30:17,607 --> 00:30:18,742
I'm still full.

413
00:30:18,742 --> 00:30:19,743
I'm not hungry yet.

414
00:30:19,743 --> 00:30:21,647
I'll put a bigger chunk of meat.

415
00:30:21,647 --> 00:30:23,139
So it will be yummier.

416
00:30:23,139 --> 00:30:24,311
- Via.
- Come on, love.

417
00:30:24,311 --> 00:30:26,750
I'm not hungry yet. I'm okay, promise.

418
00:30:26,750 --> 00:30:27,784
I'll eat after this.

419
00:30:27,784 --> 00:30:29,586
Oh, sorry.

420
00:30:29,586 --> 00:30:30,787
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

421
00:30:30,787 --> 00:30:32,255
I'll clean it up.

422
00:30:32,255 --> 00:30:34,036
Let me.

423
00:30:35,156 --> 00:30:38,128
I told you I'm not hungry yet, Via.

424
00:30:38,128 --> 00:30:40,895
Why won't you just leave me be?

425
00:30:47,237 --> 00:30:49,205
Liam, what else do I have to do?

426
00:30:49,205 --> 00:30:51,607
Via, what is your problem?

427
00:30:54,811 --> 00:30:57,881
Can you stop treating me like a child?

428
00:30:57,881 --> 00:30:59,883
You're asking me what the problem is?

429
00:30:59,883 --> 00:31:02,751
Asking me that stupid question?

430
00:31:03,720 --> 00:31:07,423
You know we have a problem, Liam.

431
00:31:09,459 --> 00:31:11,594
Can you tell me the truth?

432
00:31:13,472 --> 00:31:14,567
Are you just staying with me

433
00:31:14,567 --> 00:31:19,143
because you know
my dad might do something if we break up?

434
00:31:19,144 --> 00:31:21,812
Via, no. What are you saying?

435
00:31:21,813 --> 00:31:23,873
So do you just feel sorry for me?

436
00:31:23,873 --> 00:31:26,246
Via, no.

437
00:31:26,247 --> 00:31:28,812
Answer me, Liam!

438
00:31:28,812 --> 00:31:30,679
I don't know anymore!

439
00:31:31,982 --> 00:31:33,299
Via, I don't know anymore.

440
00:31:33,300 --> 00:31:35,185
I don't know! I'm confused!

441
00:31:35,185 --> 00:31:38,132
I just want to explode!

442
00:31:38,133 --> 00:31:41,557
I want to explode
because this is already so full!

443
00:31:41,558 --> 00:31:44,760
This is full of things I never wanted!

444
00:31:47,703 --> 00:31:50,204
Like our relationship?

445
00:32:05,448 --> 00:32:07,249
Via...

446
00:32:10,120 --> 00:32:13,522
You showed me nothing but kindness.

447
00:32:16,369 --> 00:32:18,871
So I want you to be happy.

448
00:32:22,532 --> 00:32:24,700
But I don't think...

449
00:32:26,669 --> 00:32:32,008
I'm the right person to make you feel that.

450
00:32:32,008 --> 00:32:33,510
What?

451
00:32:33,510 --> 00:32:35,078
No.

452
00:32:35,078 --> 00:32:37,443
What are you saying? Wait, what?

453
00:32:39,349 --> 00:32:40,650
Via, I'm sorry.

454
00:32:40,650 --> 00:32:42,484
Love...

455
00:32:43,887 --> 00:32:46,178
- I'm sorry.
- Liam.

456
00:33:15,300 --> 00:33:21,099
[Username: TGWTPH]
[Password]

457
00:33:21,100 --> 00:33:23,033
[The Girl with the Periwinkle Hair Channel]

458
00:33:28,567 --> 00:33:35,167
[Upload Photos/Videos]

459
00:33:35,167 --> 00:33:37,400
[Files]

460
00:33:54,006 --> 00:33:55,991
Checkmate.

461
00:34:07,751 --> 00:34:09,611
This.

462
00:34:09,611 --> 00:34:12,572
Mate.

463
00:34:15,517 --> 00:34:18,002
One more round.

464
00:34:18,002 --> 00:34:22,415
<i>And because of some unforeseen problems...</i>

465
00:34:22,415 --> 00:34:27,253
<i>I am sad to announce that my godson,</i>

466
00:34:27,253 --> 00:34:32,892
<i>the biggest action star of his generation,
Josh Pelaez,</i>

467
00:34:32,892 --> 00:34:36,220
<i>is withdrawing his candidacy.</i>

468
00:34:39,232 --> 00:34:48,507
<i>And I, your humble servant,
will continue with the fight.</i>

469
00:34:48,507 --> 00:34:55,281
<i>Today, I am announcing my candidacy...</i>

470
00:34:55,281 --> 00:34:57,159
for senator.

471
00:35:17,267 --> 00:35:23,234
[Congressman Ramon dela Peña
to run for Senator]

472
00:35:33,953 --> 00:35:36,255
Ms. Joyce, I went to the laundromat.

473
00:35:36,255 --> 00:35:38,959
I also asked Leroy to carry it for me.

474
00:35:38,959 --> 00:35:41,629
But your clothes aren't fully dry yet.

475
00:35:41,629 --> 00:35:43,896
- Should I hang it for you?
- Oh, no.

476
00:35:43,896 --> 00:35:45,631
No, I can do that.

477
00:35:45,631 --> 00:35:48,334
Go on. Go back to the set.
Our director might look for you.

478
00:35:48,334 --> 00:35:50,836
I'll take care of this.

479
00:35:50,836 --> 00:35:54,440
- Are you sure?
- Do you take a break?

480
00:35:54,440 --> 00:35:57,576
Why don't you get some rest?

481
00:35:57,576 --> 00:35:58,644
- Okay.
- Okay.

482
00:35:58,644 --> 00:36:00,779
We'll go back to the set, Miss Joyce.

483
00:36:01,747 --> 00:36:04,282
Leroy, Deedee.

484
00:36:09,989 --> 00:36:12,791
Thank you.

485
00:36:14,727 --> 00:36:18,563
Thank you for staying on in this project...

486
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:26,905
even though we had multiple setbacks.

487
00:36:29,817 --> 00:36:37,350
And even though we don't have a huge budget,
you chose to stay.

488
00:36:37,350 --> 00:36:39,284
Thank you.

489
00:36:46,507 --> 00:36:50,177
Deedee, Leroy, you're here.

490
00:36:51,224 --> 00:36:54,533
Miss Joyce, if you need anything
in your accommodation,

491
00:36:54,533 --> 00:36:55,801
just let me know.

492
00:36:55,801 --> 00:36:58,003
I don't need anything.

493
00:36:59,538 --> 00:37:03,709
I'm thanking Leroy and Deedee.

494
00:37:03,709 --> 00:37:05,710
And you, too.

495
00:37:06,846 --> 00:37:11,383
Actually, I'm grateful to
the whole production team, to everyone.

496
00:37:13,386 --> 00:37:15,387
Thank you.

497
00:37:17,890 --> 00:37:25,890
Honestly, we, the actors, owe you a lot.

498
00:37:27,466 --> 00:37:30,770
Yes, it's us that the people see.

499
00:37:30,770 --> 00:37:34,707
We represent the whole team.
We're the ones who receive the praises.

500
00:37:34,707 --> 00:37:36,975
But you, guys...

501
00:37:39,044 --> 00:37:46,919
You are the real unsung and unseen heroes
of the production.

502
00:37:46,919 --> 00:37:51,424
I'm proud to be part of this movie,
Miss Joyce.

503
00:37:51,424 --> 00:37:54,126
This is my first big project.

504
00:37:54,126 --> 00:37:57,629
My parents are so proud of me.

505
00:37:58,564 --> 00:38:00,599
As for me...

506
00:38:01,771 --> 00:38:04,537
I'm actually tired of writing movie scripts

507
00:38:04,537 --> 00:38:07,846
for Congressman Ramon in Blacksmith.

508
00:38:07,846 --> 00:38:14,547
It's always the same action movies
full of machismo.

509
00:38:14,547 --> 00:38:17,282
But you know what?

510
00:38:18,285 --> 00:38:20,981
This is the first time I felt excited again

511
00:38:20,981 --> 00:38:27,057
in writing a simple but sincere
and heartfelt story.

512
00:38:28,127 --> 00:38:36,669
Well, actually,
I think I gained the most in this project.

513
00:38:36,669 --> 00:38:40,673
Because of you and Sir Liam,

514
00:38:40,673 --> 00:38:44,944
I became passionate again in this industry.

515
00:38:44,944 --> 00:38:50,184
I've always wanted to quit
because of burnout.

516
00:38:50,184 --> 00:38:57,360
But whenever I see
how passionate you and Sir Liam are,

517
00:38:57,360 --> 00:39:00,359
I am reminded of my old self...

518
00:39:00,359 --> 00:39:02,828
Of how I used to be when I was just starting.

519
00:39:02,828 --> 00:39:09,970
All I want to do are good and relevant films.

520
00:39:13,676 --> 00:39:16,775
Sorry, I can't help but cry.

521
00:39:17,995 --> 00:39:20,663
Thank you so much.

522
00:39:21,383 --> 00:39:25,120
Seriously, thank you so much.

523
00:39:25,120 --> 00:39:29,157
This film won't be possible without you.

524
00:39:30,158 --> 00:39:32,253
Thank you.

525
00:39:32,253 --> 00:39:34,529
After this film,

526
00:39:34,529 --> 00:39:40,501
I promise, we will make more films together.

527
00:39:40,501 --> 00:39:42,304
I'd love that, Miss Joyce.

528
00:39:42,304 --> 00:39:43,505
Game!

529
00:39:43,505 --> 00:39:48,142
Okay, I'll prepare a budget
for our future projects.

530
00:39:48,142 --> 00:39:50,479
Can I have a hug?

531
00:39:50,479 --> 00:39:52,611
I'm so proud of you.

532
00:39:52,611 --> 00:39:54,359
Group hug.

533
00:39:58,186 --> 00:40:00,055
Come on, let's go.

534
00:40:00,055 --> 00:40:03,258
Miss Joyce might still have to
memorize her script.

535
00:40:03,258 --> 00:40:04,826
Go on. Go back to the set.

536
00:40:04,826 --> 00:40:06,395
- Hurry up.
- Bye, Miss Joyce.

537
00:40:06,395 --> 00:40:08,392
We'll go ahead, Miss Joyce.

538
00:40:08,392 --> 00:40:10,032
We'll get going.

539
00:40:10,032 --> 00:40:12,066
- Okay.
- Bye.

540
00:40:20,816 --> 00:40:23,597
(Thank you.)

541
00:40:25,481 --> 00:40:28,464
(Thank you.)

542
00:41:09,623 --> 00:41:13,494
Liam, are you okay?
How long have you been there?

543
00:41:13,494 --> 00:41:14,863
Wait, are we going to
shoot my scenes already?

544
00:41:14,863 --> 00:41:18,033
Sorry, I didn't notice you.

545
00:41:20,628 --> 00:41:22,328
Joyce...

546
00:41:23,343 --> 00:41:25,992
There's something I want to tell you.

547
00:41:29,210 --> 00:41:30,345
What is it?

548
00:41:30,345 --> 00:41:31,828
I can't help it anymore.

549
00:41:31,828 --> 00:41:33,773
What?

550
00:41:33,773 --> 00:41:37,452
I can't bear this anymore, Joyce.
I feel like exploding.

551
00:41:37,452 --> 00:41:40,889
- Where? Which?
- Can you let me talk first?

552
00:41:44,258 --> 00:41:45,586
Okay.

553
00:41:45,586 --> 00:41:47,171
Joyce...

554
00:41:49,064 --> 00:41:51,433
I just want to let you know that...

555
00:41:53,570 --> 00:41:56,138
before we worked together...

556
00:41:57,519 --> 00:42:02,990
I was at the point in my life
where I was lost.

557
00:42:06,167 --> 00:42:08,035
And you...

558
00:42:11,006 --> 00:42:15,357
You taught me how to find myself.

559
00:42:17,126 --> 00:42:19,029
Joyce...

560
00:42:22,895 --> 00:42:25,330
Joyce...

561
00:42:25,330 --> 00:42:28,333
I don't know where I'll be without you.

562
00:42:30,403 --> 00:42:32,471
Me, too, Liam.

563
00:42:34,206 --> 00:42:38,343
I'm also happy to be working with you.

564
00:42:39,812 --> 00:42:43,515
Wait. Where is this headed?

565
00:42:44,234 --> 00:42:46,065
I love you.

566
00:42:52,424 --> 00:42:54,792
I love you, Joyce.

567
00:43:00,399 --> 00:43:04,202
I loved you the first time I saw you.

568
00:43:16,415 --> 00:43:19,771
The first time you saw me?

569
00:43:20,537 --> 00:43:22,124
A few months ago?

570
00:43:22,124 --> 00:43:24,959
No.

571
00:43:25,837 --> 00:43:27,771
It's been a long time.

572
00:43:28,393 --> 00:43:32,096
It's been a long time, Joyce.
I have loved you for a long time.

573
00:43:33,599 --> 00:43:37,001
And even though a lot has already happened
in our lives...

574
00:43:37,703 --> 00:43:40,238
I still love you.

575
00:43:46,643 --> 00:43:48,778
Liam, I can't...

576
00:43:49,748 --> 00:43:51,950
I can't understand.

577
00:43:51,950 --> 00:43:54,419
It's hard to explain.

578
00:43:58,357 --> 00:44:00,291
But I love you.

579
00:44:34,726 --> 00:44:36,125
Joyce...

580
00:45:08,060 --> 00:45:10,735
Joyce, we're now at the hospital.

581
00:45:10,735 --> 00:45:12,133
Hang in there, please.

582
00:45:12,133 --> 00:45:14,219
Your dad is here too.

583
00:45:14,219 --> 00:45:15,467
What did you do?

584
00:45:15,467 --> 00:45:21,446
That's how I can protect myself
from Joyce's revelation.

585
00:45:21,446 --> 00:45:25,777
Deep inside your heart,
that's what you want, too.

586
00:45:25,777 --> 00:45:27,746
For that woman to be gone.

587
00:45:27,746 --> 00:45:29,481
What happened to my daughter?

588
00:45:29,481 --> 00:45:32,417
I have no one to blame but you!

589
00:45:32,417 --> 00:45:36,221
What happened?

590
00:45:36,221 --> 00:45:37,924
What happened?

591
00:45:37,924 --> 00:45:39,743
What?
